    "rawMarkdown": "Ya I think you should publish it...the community would definitely find a 60% coverage pseudolabeled dataset useful  either for pre-training or as features for Level-2 stacking models..but I think you should be careful relying on the standard 'accuracy.' because medical datasets usually have huge class imbalances since most scans are normal the 97% accuracy you have might actually result in a poor leaderboard score if it's missing the minority positive cases and I think you should test the pseudolabels against the competition's official ROC AUC metric first.",
